From: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: bq25890: do not signal userspace from the property read path

bq25890_power_supply_get_property() calls bq25890_update_state(), which runs
the IRQ handler body ("in case we lost an interrupt"). When the chip state
differs from the cached one, that body calls power_supply_changed(). Building
the resulting uevent (power_supply_uevent -> add_prop_uevent) reads EVERY
property, each read again runs the handler body, and as long as the chip state
keeps changing between two reads the uevent re-queues itself:

  power_supply_changed <- __bq25890_handle_irq <- bq25890_update_state
    <- bq25890_power_supply_get_property <- power_supply_format_property
    <- add_prop_uevent <- power_supply_uevent <- kobject_uevent
    <- power_supply_changed_work

That is a self-sustaining uevent/IRQ loop whenever the charger's state keeps
changing.

Fix: the property read path still refreshes the cached state but no longer
calls power_supply_changed(); the IRQ handler (and the optional poll work)
keep signalling. Limitation: a change first seen by a property read is not
signalled by that read.

Signed-off-by: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq25890_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq25890_charger.c
@@ -451,7 +451,7 @@
 	}
 }
 
-static irqreturn_t __bq25890_handle_irq(struct bq25890_device *bq);
+static irqreturn_t __bq25890_handle_irq(struct bq25890_device *bq, bool notify);
 
 static int bq25890_get_vbus_voltage(struct bq25890_device *bq)
 {
@@ -472,8 +472,12 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&bq->lock);
-	/* update state in case we lost an interrupt */
-	__bq25890_handle_irq(bq);
+	/*
+	 * update state in case we lost an interrupt. Do not signal userspace from
+	 * here: building the uevent reads every property, which lands here, and
+	 * a flapping chip state then re-queues the uevent forever.
+	 */
+	__bq25890_handle_irq(bq, false);
 	*state = bq->state;
 	do_adc_conv = (!state->online || state->hiz) && bq25890_is_adc_property(psp);
 	if (do_adc_conv)
@@ -814,7 +818,7 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static irqreturn_t __bq25890_handle_irq(struct bq25890_device *bq)
+static irqreturn_t __bq25890_handle_irq(struct bq25890_device *bq, bool notify)
 {
 	bool adc_conv_rate, new_adc_conv_rate;
 	struct bq25890_state new_state;
@@ -849,7 +853,8 @@
 	}
 
 	bq->state = new_state;
-	power_supply_changed(bq->charger);
+	if (notify)
+		power_supply_changed(bq->charger);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 error:
@@ -864,7 +869,7 @@
 	irqreturn_t ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&bq->lock);
-	ret = __bq25890_handle_irq(bq);
+	ret = __bq25890_handle_irq(bq, true);
 	mutex_unlock(&bq->lock);
 
 	return ret;
